{"ld": 858, "paper": "HP544", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Ensure Behavioral and Mental Health Services Are Available to Students by Providing Grants to Schools That Contract for Those Services", "sponsor_id": "h-gramlich-lori", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-brennan-michael", "h-crockett-edward", "h-dodge-janice", "h-murphy-kelly", "h-sargent-holly"], "committee_code": "EDU", "committee_name": "Education and Cultural Affairs", "summary": {"text": "3239 This bill establishes a grant program within the Department of Education to provide grants to school administrative units that contract for behavioral and mental health services provided by licensed behavioral and mental health service providers. The bill limits the use of funds provided through the grant program to behavioral and mental health services that are not otherwise covered or reimbursable through the MaineCare program and provides that funds must be used in a manner that does not supplant qualified and available school administrative unit behavioral and mental health staff. The bill also provides that the amounts of the grants must be based on a school administrative unit's population and provides ongoing funding for the grants starting in fiscal year 2025-26.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0544&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "final_disposition": {"label": "Enacted", "date": "2026-01-11", "governor_action": "Unsigned", "governor_action_date": "2026-01-11"}, "fiscal_status": "Fiscal Impact", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 858)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0544&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-289)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0544&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}, {"label": "Amendment S-A (S-464)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0544&item=4&snum=132", "i